<title>SPAIN: Spain approves 60 pct Auxini sale to OCP.</title>
<headline>Spain approves 60 pct Auxini sale to OCP.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government approved on Friday the sale of a 60 percent stake in Auximi by the state holding company SEPI to Spanish builders OCP Construcciones for 5.93 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>SEPI said the price was 30.1 percent higher than the previous sell off. OCP already has 40 percent of Auxini.</p>
<p>Auxini had a 1996 turnover of 57.3 billion pesetas, with profit at 1.2 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>OCP announced on Wednesday a merger with another Spanish construction company Gines Navarro.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
